Datasets exported to NetCDF can now be compressed using the deflate (gzip) compression
built into NetCDF4/HDF5. Depending on the data this reduces the size of the exported
files by a factor of roughly 1.3 to 3.3 with no measurable slowdown of the export, and
no loss of precision since the compression is lossless. Compressed files remain regular
NetCDF files that can be read by any NetCDF client without any special handling.

Compression is disabled by default for now and can be enabled with the new
``qcodes.config.dataset.export_netcdf_compression_level`` config option, which sets the
compression level between ``0`` (uncompressed, the default) and ``9``. A level of ``4``
is recommended since higher levels are significantly slower while giving almost no
additional size reduction. We plan to enable compression by default in a future
release, so please try it out and let us know about any problems.
